{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-138593",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the sample mean vector is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ are the individual observations (columns of $X$).\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{4}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{4}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
